        {
          "id": 3197078070,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "There is not Coverity warning related to `proto_tree_add_item_ret_uint8()`, that is why I only add this minor change to `proto_tree_add_item_ret_uint16()` only.\n\nMost static analysis engines (including Coverity 2024.12) have a built-in \"threshold of insignificance\" for taint. A uint8_t has a maximum value of 255. Even if the value is \"tainted\" (from the network), a loop that runs a maximum of 255 times is mathematically incapable of causing a CPU hang or a significant memory exhaustion event in a modern system like Wireshark. Therefore, the analyzer often silently drops the \"Tainted Scalar\" tracking for 8-bit variables because they don't meet the \"severity\" bar for a security defect.",
          "author": {
            "id": 20971927,
            "username": "rtommy",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tamas Regos",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/20971927/avatar.png?v=1788090511",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rtommy"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-03-27T09:16:55.769Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-03-27T09:18:07.372Z",
          "system": false,
