        {
          "id": 3197751457,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "`proto_tree_add_item_ret_uint16` is based on `proto_tree_add_item_ret_uint` which taints `val32`. So simply cast `(uint16_t)val32` won't change that. However, bitwise AND 0xFFFF clears the taint since it basically provides a max value of it. Yes, the byte swapping has part of the taint for sure and that is another reason why xxx_uint8 is not tainted.\n\nOther way would be\n```\nuint32_t num;\n...\nif (num > UINT16_MAX) num = UINT16_MAX;\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 20971927,
            "username": "rtommy",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tamas Regos",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
