        {
          "id": 3197782071,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Coverity uses Heuristics to identify untrusted data (Heuristic-based Taint Analysis). Yes, clear.\n\nCoverity's engine assumes that if you are byte-swapping, you are almost certainly processing external network headers. Therefore, the result of a byte-swap is automatically \"Poisoned\" or \"Tainted\". Yes, clear.\n\n8-bit values don't require swapping, they never trigger this specific heuristic. Yes, clear.\n\nWhile a `uint16_t` type naturally restricts the value to `0xFFFF`, Coverity's engine requires an explicit Sanitization Event (like a bitmask or a saturating guard) to clear the 'Taint' flag from the dataflow before it hits a loop bound for example.",
          "author": {
            "id": 20971927,
            "username": "rtommy",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tamas Regos",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/20971927/avatar.png?v=1788090511",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rtommy"
